From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: A733 combo-PHY -- swing and pre-emphasis through phy_configure()

`phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-rate-2700` and `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-bracket-the-dp-rate-table` gave this PHY a .configure that carries the rate and the lane count.
The third arm, set_voltages, was refused:

    if (dp->set_voltages) {
            dev_warn_once(cp->dev,
                          "DP swing/pre-emphasis not implemented, link training cannot complete\n");
            return -EOPNOTSUPP;
    }

That was an honest refusal and it was also a hard blocker: link training IS the
swing/pre-emphasis loop. A DisplayPort source reads the sink's adjust request,
drives what it asked for, and reads again -- with this arm refused, the loop
cannot get past clock recovery on any lane the sink is not already happy with.
This patch implements it.

THE SEQUENCE IS MAINLINE'S, THE VALUES ARE THE BOARD'S
-------------------------------------------------------

This PHY is a Cadence Torrent derivative and cdns_torrent_dp_set_voltages()
(drivers/phy/cadence/phy-cadence-torrent.c:1558) is the sequence register for
register. Five registers per lane, in this order, and the first and last are a
freeze/thaw bracket whose REASON mainline states in words rather than leaving to
be guessed at (:1568-1571, :1592-1595): TX_DIAG_ACYA[0] set "to freeze the
current state of the analog TX driver", cleared "to allow the state of analog TX
driver to reflect the new programmed one". So the four coefficient writes land
atomically as far as the analog front end is concerned.

⚠ That bracket is NOT `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-reset-sequence`'s reset bracket and must not be confused with it.
Swing changes happen on a LIVE link between two training rounds; tearing the
link down there would destroy the thing being trained. The rate and lane writes
keep the reset bracket, set_voltages gets the ACYA one, and .configure now runs
them as three independent arms in mainline's order -- lanes, rate, voltages
(phy-cadence-torrent.c:1602-1637).

The five register indices are mainline's own constants offset by the lane-CDB
base: 0x4000 + lane * 0x200 + {0x0040, 0x004C, 0x0050, 0x00C6, 0x01E7}. The
cross-check that they are the same registers is `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-rate-2700`'s own rate table, which
already carries the absolute results (0x4040/0x4240/0x4440/0x4640 for
TX_TXCC_CTRL, 0x4050.. for MGNFS).

WHERE THE COEFFICIENT VALUES COME FROM -- NOT ONE SOURCE, SO NOT ONE CLAIM
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

There is no UM field table for these registers at all: the vendor's
trilinear_dp14.h is a bare offset list and the PMA is Cadence's, not
Allwinner's. So the table is stated cell by cell:

  (0,0), (1,0)  EXERCISED ON SILICON. Training starts at (0,0); the sink asked
                for swing 1 on all four lanes and four lanes then reached CR in
                one round and EQ in one round, 77 77 01 01, all four symbol-error
                counters valid at zero, and a picture.
  (2,0)         READ BACK off a live vendor four-lane link: the four MGNFS words
                read 0x0010 0x000E 0x000E 0x0010, which is this row to the digit
                (the same four are the "4 disagree" entries in
                `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-rate-2700`'s cross-check, and they
                disagree precisely because they are the values training owns).
  the rest      vendor dp_lv_table_2g7 -- a HINT, not verified, and marked as
                such in the code rather than presented as known.
  (2,1)         the weakest: it is the one LEGAL DP cell that our shell script
                a733-dp-link-train.sh (a user-space training script used before
                this driver; not part of this recipe) never names, so it falls
                into that script's catch-all together with the illegal ones.
                Carried from there, unexercised.

WHERE THE VENDOR DRIVER DIFFERS, AND WHAT THIS DOES INSTEAD
------------------------------------------------------------

  vendor                                   | ours
  -----------------------------------------+------------------------------------
  per-lane index taken from sysfs straight | bounds-checked in the PROVIDER, the
  into dp_lv_table[sw][pre], no bound      | way cdns_torrent_dp_verify_config()
                                           | does: each level 0..3 AND their sum
                                           | at most 3 (DP 1.4 Table 3-1), with
                                           | -ERANGE and the offending lane named
  trilinear_set_lane_sw_pre() -- an EMPTY  | no such slot; the swing lives where
  function registered in the ops table     | the hardware is, in the PHY
  varies DRV_DIAG_TX_DRV with pre-emphasis | kept -- here the vendor's values
  where mainline pins it at 0x0003         | match this board and mainline's
                                           | generic table does not
  illegal cells: repeats the last legal row| kept, rather than mainline's
                                           | 0xFFFF placeholders. Unreachable
                                           | twice over (the check above, and the
                                           | DP driver clamps before asking), so
                                           | it is a third belt, not a path

⚠ And one defect in OUR OWN shell instrument, which this table fixes:
a733-dp-link-train.sh has a single catch-all arm serving both the legal cell
(2,1) and every illegal one, so swing 3 with any pre-emphasis gets the (2,1) row
instead of repeating (3,0). Unreachable in practice and still not what a reader
of that script would predict.

WHAT IS STILL REFUSED, BY NAME
------------------------------

Every link rate except 2700 Mb/s, and SSC. There is one PMA rate table; a swing
table for a rate that cannot be configured would be dead code that looks like
rate support, so the 1620 Mb/s swing table is deliberately NOT here either.

⚠ NOT HARDWARE-PROVEN, AND THE BOARD RUN THAT LOOKED LIKE IT MIGHT PROVE IT DID
NOT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A test boot on the 8 GiB board, 2026-08-19, carried this patch, proved `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-lane-map-and-inverts` outright and
proved nothing here. Nothing in that session read a drive level this patch had
written: the one MGNFS reading taken was at the wrong address (below), and the
training attempts made after the Type-C recovery could not exercise it either --
that recovery had left DP alt mode, so the four COMB0 lanes were in reset and
there was no link for a drive level to act on. The same failure reproduced on
`dp545`, a kernel WITHOUT these patches, which rules them out as its cause.

⚠ RECOVERY IS A POWER CYCLE, not an unbind/bind of the rt1711h i2c device: its
second use that day left DP alt mode outright and the kernel then wedged with RCU
stalls on one CPU until the board was power-cycled anyway.

⚠ The MGNFS reading taken in that session ("still zero") was taken at
0x06C98xxx, which is NOT TX_TXCC_MGNFS_MULT_000. The register is at
0x06C80000 + ((0x4000 + lane*0x200 + 0x50) << 1) = 0x06C880A0 / 0x06C884A0 /
0x06C888A0 / 0x06C88CA0 -- the PMA base
(A733 user manual, chapter 2 Memory Map, COMBPHY0), the index
from what a733_combophy_dp_set_voltages() writes and from `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-rate-2700`'s rate table,
which carries the same four indices (0x4050/0x4250/0x4450/0x4650) as absolute
results. So that reading says nothing about this patch in either direction.

WHAT IT OWES
------------

  1. A link that trains from the driver. Observable: with `drm-a733-dp-link-training` in the same
     kernel, `echo 0 > /sys/kernel/debug/5740000.displayport/train` returns 0
     and DPCD 0x202/0x203 read 0x77 0x77 with 0x204 bit0 set.
     Falsified by: phy_configure() still returning -EOPNOTSUPP, or CR never
     completing on a board and cable where the shell script
     a733-dp-link-train.sh does complete it.
  2. The registers this patch writes, read back at a known level. Observable:
     after training settles at swing 1 / pre 0 on all four lanes (which is what
     the 8 GiB board + the bench sink asked for on 2026-08-18), the four MGNFS words
     0x06C880A0 / 0x06C884A0 / 0x06C888A0 / 0x06C88CA0 read 0x001F001F,
     0x001E001E, 0x001E001E, 0x001F001F (16-bit values mirrored into both halves
     of a 32-bit read).
     Falsified by: 0x002A002A, which is what `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-rate-2700`'s rate table leaves behind and
     therefore means set_voltages never ran.
  3. ⚠ A SUPERSPEED RE-PROOF. This patch adds PMA writes to the driver that owns
     COMB0 and RST_BUS_SERDES is shared. Observable: on a boot with NO DP sink
     attached, `lsusb -t` still shows a SuperSpeed device at 10000M, and
     LINK_CTRL0 0x06C01000 still reads 0x00000111.
     Falsified by: SuperSpeed dropping, or any of the five per-lane registers
     moving on a port that never entered DP alt mode.

NOT HARDWARE-PROVEN -- and see the section above: the 2026-08-19 test boot
carried this patch, proved `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-lane-map-and-inverts`, and settled nothing here. Builds clean at W=1
with the debug instrumentation both on and off; checkpatch 0/0.

The coefficient cells marked as vendor values come from
dp_lv_table_2g7 in drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c from
radxa/allwinner-bsp (commit b36af3872d4e, "aiot-linux-v1.4.6 release"; the
file is unchanged on the branches cubie-aiot-v1.4.6 and cubie-aiot-v1.4.8),
GPL-2.0, Copyright(c) 2020 - 2023 Allwinner Technology Co.,Ltd. and
Copyright (C) 2024 Allwinner Electronics Co., Ltd.:
https://github.com/radxa/allwinner-bsp/blob/b36af3872d4e6e91da6e929f4ccf4822b3ea9d66/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
The write sequence follows cdns_torrent_dp_set_voltages() in
drivers/phy/cadence/phy-cadence-torrent.c (Linux 6.18, GPL-2.0-only,
Copyright 2018 Cadence Design Systems, Inc.).

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
@@ -151,6 +151,42 @@
 #define A733_DP_LANE_INVERT_DEFAULT	GENMASK(A733_DP_LANES - 1, 0)
 #define A733_DP_LANE_MAP_IDENTITY	0x00003210
 
+/*
+ * The PMA's per-lane transmit CDB. The five register indices below are
+ * mainline's own Cadence Torrent constants -- this PHY is a Torrent derivative
+ * and its swing/pre-emphasis sequence is cdns_torrent_dp_set_voltages()
+ * register for register (drivers/phy/cadence/phy-cadence-torrent.c:1558). The
+ * lane-CDB base 0x4000 and the 0x200-word lane stride are what turn them into
+ * the absolute indices `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-rate-2700`'s own rate table already carries (0x4040, 0x4240,
+ * 0x4440, 0x4640 for TX_TXCC_CTRL), which is the cross-check that they are the
+ * same registers:
+ *
+ *   TX_TXCC_CTRL           0x0040   phy-cadence-torrent.c:169
+ *   TX_TXCC_CPOST_MULT_00  0x004C   :170
+ *   TX_TXCC_MGNFS_MULT_000 0x0050   :172
+ *   DRV_DIAG_TX_DRV        0x00C6   :174
+ *   TX_DIAG_ACYA           0x01E7   :186
+ *
+ * ⚠ Byte offset = word index << 1, and the block is 16 bits wide -- a 32-bit
+ * read shows every value mirrored into both halves.
+ */
+#define PMA_TX_CDB(lane, idx)		(((0x4000 + (lane) * 0x200 + (idx)) << 1))
+#define PMA_TX_TXCC_CTRL		0x0040
+#define  PMA_TX_TXCC_CTRL_VAL		0x08A4	/* identical to mainline's constant */
+#define PMA_TX_TXCC_CPOST_MULT_00	0x004C
+#define PMA_TX_TXCC_MGNFS_MULT_000	0x0050
+#define PMA_DRV_DIAG_TX_DRV		0x00C6
+#define PMA_TX_DIAG_ACYA		0x01E7
+#define  PMA_TX_DIAG_ACYA_HBDC		BIT(0)
+
+/* DP 1.4 Table 3-1: four swing levels, four pre-emphasis levels, and their sum
+ * may not exceed 3. Both bounds are enforced in this provider, the way
+ * cdns_torrent_dp_verify_config() does (phy-cadence-torrent.c:1405-1417) --
+ * the vendor takes a per-lane index straight from sysfs into dp_lv_table[sw][pre]
+ * with no bound at all.
+ */
+#define A733_DP_LEVEL_MAX		3
+
 #define SERDES_REFCLK_RATE		100000000	/* serdes-phy-cfg = 100 MHz */
 #define PHY_LOCK_TIMEOUT_US		2000
 #define PMA_READY_TIMEOUT_US		10000
@@ -927,6 +963,133 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * One cell of the transmit de-emphasis table: the three Torrent coefficient
+ * registers, with MGNFS carried PER LANE because on this board it is per lane.
+ *
+ * WHERE THESE NUMBERS COME FROM, cell by cell, because it is not one source:
+ *
+ *   (0,0), (1,0)  exercised on silicon. Training starts at (0,0) and the sink
+ *                 asked for swing 1 on all four lanes; four lanes then reached
+ *                 CR in one round and EQ in one round, 77 77 01 01, zero symbol
+ *                 errors, and a picture. The rows below say for
+ *                 each other cell whether it was read back or
+ *                 carried.
+ *   (2,0)         READ BACK off a live vendor four-lane link on the 8 GiB board: the four
+ *                 MGNFS words read 0x0010 0x000E 0x000E 0x0010, which is this
+ *                 row to the digit (`phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-rate-2700`'s row; the
+ *                 capture is not tracked in this tree).
+ *                 That is a register read on silicon, not a value out of code.
+ *   the rest      vendor dp_lv_table_2g7, i.e. a HINT that has not been
+ *                 verified. Marked as such rather than presented as known: no
+ *                 UM field table exists for these registers at all.
+ *
+ *   (2,1)         the weakest of all -- it is the one valid DP cell that
+ *                 the shell script this replaces never names, so it falls into
+ *                 that script's catch-all arm together with the ILLEGAL cells.
+ *                 The values are carried from there and are unexercised.
+ *
+ * ⚠ The illegal cells (voltage + pre > 3) repeat the last legal row of their
+ * swing, which is the vendor's behaviour, where mainline's
+ * vltg_coeff[][] writes 0xFFFF into them (phy-cadence-torrent.c:646-649). They
+ * are unreachable twice over -- a733_combophy_dp_check() refuses the request and
+ * the DP driver clamps before asking -- so this is a third belt, not a path.
+ *
+ * ⚠ The shell script this replaces gets the illegal cells wrong in a way a table
+ * cannot: its single catch-all gives swing 3 with any pre-emphasis the (2,1)
+ * row instead of repeating (3,0). Unreachable, and still not what a reader of
+ * that script would predict.
+ *
+ * ⬜ Still open, and named rather than guessed: lanes 1 and 2 sit one MGNFS step
+ * below lanes 0 and 3 in every row. That reads like trace-length compensation
+ * and nothing in the vendor tree says so -- no comment, no changelog, no
+ * reference measurement.
+ */
+struct a733_dp_swing {
+	u16	diag_tx_drv;
+	u16	cpost_mult;
+	u16	mgnfs_mult[A733_DP_LANES];
+};
+
+/* [voltage swing][pre-emphasis], 2700 Mb/s. The 1620 Mb/s table is NOT here:
+ * this PHY has no 1620 PMA table either, so a swing table for a rate that
+ * cannot be configured would be dead code that looks like rate support.
+ */
+static const struct a733_dp_swing a733_dp_swing_2700[4][4] = {
+	/* swing 0 */
+	{ { 0x0003, 0x0000, { 0x0028, 0x0026, 0x0026, 0x0028 } },
+	  { 0x00B2, 0x0008, { 0x0024, 0x0023, 0x0023, 0x0024 } },
+	  { 0x00B2, 0x0016, { 0x001C, 0x001B, 0x001B, 0x001C } },
+	  { 0x00B2, 0x0023, { 0x000B, 0x000A, 0x000A, 0x000B } } },
+	/* swing 1 -- (1,3) is illegal and repeats (1,2) */
+	{ { 0x0003, 0x0000, { 0x001F, 0x001E, 0x001E, 0x001F } },
+	  { 0x00B2, 0x000A, { 0x001A, 0x0019, 0x0019, 0x001A } },
+	  { 0x00B2, 0x0019, { 0x000A, 0x0009, 0x0009, 0x000A } },
+	  { 0x00B2, 0x0019, { 0x000A, 0x0009, 0x0009, 0x000A } } },
+	/* swing 2 -- (2,2) and (2,3) are illegal and repeat (2,1) */
+	{ { 0x0003, 0x0000, { 0x0010, 0x000E, 0x000E, 0x0010 } },
+	  { 0x0082, 0x0011, { 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000 } },
+	  { 0x0082, 0x0011, { 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000 } },
+	  { 0x0082, 0x0011, { 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000 } } },
+	/* swing 3 -- everything but (3,0) is illegal and repeats it */
+	{ { 0x0003, 0x0000, { 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000 } },
+	  { 0x0003, 0x0000, { 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000 } },
+	  { 0x0003, 0x0000, { 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000 } },
+	  { 0x0003, 0x0000, { 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000, 0x0000 } } },
+};
+
+/*
+ * Apply the swing and pre-emphasis each lane was asked for.
+ *
+ * THE FREEZE/THAW BRACKET IS THE POINT, and it is not `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-reset-sequence`'s reset bracket --
+ * this runs on a LIVE link, between two training rounds, and tearing the link
+ * down here would destroy the thing being trained. TX_DIAG_ACYA[0] is what
+ * makes that safe, and mainline says why in words this driver does not have to
+ * guess at: bit set "to freeze the current state of the analog TX driver",
+ * cleared "to allow the state of analog TX driver to reflect the new programmed
+ * one" (phy-cadence-torrent.c:1568-1571, :1592-1595). So the four coefficient
+ * writes land atomically as far as the analog front end is concerned and the
+ * output never walks through an intermediate drive level.
+ *
+ * ⚠ The rate table leaves MGNFS at 0x002A on all four lanes -- mainline's
+ * generic swing-0 value, not this board's. So a link that has just had its rate
+ * configured is at a drive level nothing measured; the first thing training does
+ * is call this with swing 0 / pre 0 on every lane, which is also what puts the
+ * source and the sink at the same starting level.
+ */
+static void a733_combophy_dp_set_voltages(struct a733_combophy *cp,
+					  const struct phy_configure_opts_dp *dp)
+{
+	unsigned int lane;
+
+	for (lane = 0; lane < dp->lanes; lane++) {
+		const struct a733_dp_swing *row =
+			&a733_dp_swing_2700[dp->voltage[lane]][dp->pre[lane]];
+		void __iomem *acya = cp->pma +
+				     PMA_TX_CDB(lane, PMA_TX_DIAG_ACYA);
+		u16 v;
+
+		v = readw(acya);
+		writew(v | PMA_TX_DIAG_ACYA_HBDC, acya);
+
+		writew(PMA_TX_TXCC_CTRL_VAL,
+		       cp->pma + PMA_TX_CDB(lane, PMA_TX_TXCC_CTRL));
+		writew(row->diag_tx_drv,
+		       cp->pma + PMA_TX_CDB(lane, PMA_DRV_DIAG_TX_DRV));
+		/* MGNFS is indexed by the PHYSICAL lane as well as by the level:
+		 * the per-lane skew belongs to the board, the level to what that
+		 * lane asked for.
+		 */
+		writew(row->mgnfs_mult[lane],
+		       cp->pma + PMA_TX_CDB(lane, PMA_TX_TXCC_MGNFS_MULT_000));
+		writew(row->cpost_mult,
+		       cp->pma + PMA_TX_CDB(lane, PMA_TX_TXCC_CPOST_MULT_00));
+
+		v = readw(acya);
+		writew(v & ~PMA_TX_DIAG_ACYA_HBDC, acya);
+	}
+}
+
+/*
  * Is this rate/lane request one the driver can carry out? Split out of
  * .configure so that .validate can answer the same question with no side
  * effects, which is what phy.h requires of it: "It must not change any actual
@@ -939,6 +1102,8 @@
  */
 static int a733_combophy_dp_check(const struct phy_configure_opts_dp *dp)
 {
+	unsigned int i;
+
 	if (dp->set_rate) {
 		if (dp->link_rate != DP_LINK_RATE_HBR_MBPS || dp->ssc)
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
@@ -949,9 +1114,64 @@
 			return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/* set_voltages names its lanes through the SAME `lanes` field even when
+	 * set_lanes is clear ("Only lanes specified by 'lanes' parameter will be
+	 * affected", include/linux/phy/phy-dp.h), so it has to be checked here
+	 * too -- otherwise a swing-only request with a stale lane count indexes
+	 * past the four the PMA has.
+	 */
+	if (dp->set_voltages) {
+		if (!dp->lanes || dp->lanes > A733_DP_LANES)
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < dp->lanes; i++)
+			if (dp->voltage[i] > A733_DP_LEVEL_MAX ||
+			    dp->pre[i] > A733_DP_LEVEL_MAX ||
+			    dp->voltage[i] + dp->pre[i] > A733_DP_LEVEL_MAX)
+				return -ERANGE;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Say which half was refused and with which number. Split out because
+ * .configure has three refusal cases now and .validate must have none -- a rate
+ * ladder that asks before it acts would otherwise print a line per rung.
+ *
+ * ⚠ Only the field the consumer actually SET is printed. union
+ * phy_configure_opts is routinely left partly uninitialised by its callers
+ * (dw-dp.c:559 declares it on the stack and fills three fields), so printing
+ * dp->lanes for a rate-only request would be printing whatever was on that
+ * stack.
+ */
+static void a733_combophy_dp_refused(struct a733_combophy *cp,
+				     const struct phy_configure_opts_dp *dp,
+				     int ret)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	switch (ret) {
+	case -EOPNOTSUPP:
+		dev_warn(cp->dev,
+			 "DP link rate %u Mb/s%s refused: only %u Mb/s without SSC has a PMA table\n",
+			 dp->link_rate, dp->ssc ? " with SSC" : "",
+			 DP_LINK_RATE_HBR_MBPS);
+		return;
+	case -EINVAL:
+		dev_warn(cp->dev,
+			 "DP lane count %u refused: the PMA lane word encodes 1, 2 or 4\n",
+			 dp->lanes);
+		return;
+	case -ERANGE:
+		for (i = 0; i < dp->lanes && i < A733_DP_LANES; i++)
+			dev_warn(cp->dev,
+				 "DP lane %u swing %u / pre-emphasis %u refused: DP 1.4 Table 3-1 allows each 0..%u and their sum at most %u\n",
+				 i, dp->voltage[i], dp->pre[i],
+				 A733_DP_LEVEL_MAX, A733_DP_LEVEL_MAX);
+		return;
+	}
+}
+
 /*
  * phy_ops.configure is how a DisplayPort controller asks for a link rate and a
  * lane count, and on the real alt-mode path that controller is the DP
@@ -975,10 +1195,51 @@
  * 0x100 while the PMA stayed at 2.7 Gbps is what an earlier
  * measurement found: RBR fails at any lane count.
  *
- * What is still not implemented, and is refused rather than half-applied: the
- * swing/pre-emphasis tables (combo0_dp_set_sw_pre), and every link rate except
- * 2700 Mb/s.
+ * SWING/PRE-EMPHASIS IS NOT IN THAT BRACKET, deliberately. It is applied on a
+ * live link between two training rounds and carries its own, much smaller
+ * bracket -- TX_DIAG_ACYA, see a733_combophy_dp_set_voltages(). Putting it
+ * inside the reset staircase would tear down the link training is converging.
+ * Mainline's Torrent driver makes the same split: set_lanes, set_rate and
+ * set_voltages are three independent arms of one .configure call, in that order
+ * (phy-cadence-torrent.c:1602-1637).
+ *
+ * What is still not implemented, and is refused rather than half-applied: every
+ * link rate except 2700 Mb/s, and SSC.
  */
+/* The rate/lane half of .configure, inside `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-reset-sequence`'s reset bracket. Caller holds
+ * cp->lock.
+ *
+ * Lane count first and the rate table last, which is the order the vendor
+ * reaches (combo0_dp_set_lanes() then combo0_dp_set_rate() in its .configure)
+ * -- with one difference: the vendor writes the lane word into a LIVE PMA,
+ * outside any bracket. It is inside ours, because a PMA write into a live PHY is
+ * what cost a board an SError on 2026-08-18 and nothing says this word is
+ * exempt.
+ */
+static int a733_combophy_dp_apply_link(struct a733_combophy *cp,
+				       const struct phy_configure_opts_dp *dp)
+{
+	int ret = 0;
